WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.010
The agency's cloud
decides what it can use,

2
00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:07.275
so this book dates every product
statement to October 2026.

3
00:00:07.275 --> 00:00:12.811
The core Agent ID platform, with
blueprints, agent identities and sponsors,

4
00:00:12.811 --> 00:00:16.650
was announced as generally
available in April 2026.

5
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.196
But several controls are still preview,

6
00:00:19.196 --> 00:00:22.437
including agent targeting
in Conditional Access.

7
00:00:22.437 --> 00:00:23.726
The slide lists them.

8
00:00:23.726 --> 00:00:25.937
The government clouds
are the bigger issue.

9
00:00:25.937 --> 00:00:31.551
GCC has a partial, documented subset:
identity and access governance for agents,

10
00:00:31.551 --> 00:00:36.313
but not Microsoft's audit, data loss
prevention or network controls.

11
00:00:36.313 --> 00:00:39.570
GCC High and DOD have no
published availability,

12
00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:43.969
so treat agent identities as
unavailable there until Microsoft

13
00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:48.612
confirms otherwise in writing, and
govern AI as workload identities.

14
00:00:48.612 --> 00:00:52.903
The rule is simple: build on what's
generally available in your own cloud,

15
00:00:52.903 --> 00:00:55.375
and keep preview features as watch items.

16
00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:57.940
Next, the person behind each agent.
